{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Persistence is Key"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Notes About Resume"}, {"type": "position", "content": 2}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 10}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify and describe issues relating to money, in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts"}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le10ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " What Clauses and Long Phrases as Subject"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You shift emphasis from the beginning to another part of the sentence by using <span class=\"italic\">what</span> , <span class=\"italic\">that </span> and <span class=\"italic\">who </span> phrases as subjects."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Usually, we focus on the person doing the action in this case.<br/> <span class=\"italic\">  Example: I really need to focus on writing an effective resume.</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "If we wish to place emphasis on another part of the sentence, we isolate that part and package up the rest of the information into a what-phrase (or sometimes a that clause.)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Example: What I really need is to focus on writing an effective one. </span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">What </span> </span> or <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">Who </span> </span> serves as a placeholder for the content of the noun phrase that has been moved to the end of the sentence. The effect is that more emphasis is placed on the initial content.<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Example: </span> <ul><span class=\"italic\"><li>What I really liked about the workshop is that the tips were really on point. </li> <li>What a resume should do is help you land an interview.</li> </span> </ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "This is how we form \u201cWhat\u201d clauses. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> subject / What-phrase</div> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" be \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">complement</div> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">The first thing we need to work on<br/> What you want to present<br/> What a friend had told me<br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">What you are saying </span></span> </div> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">is <br/> is<br/> is<br/>is</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">the layout.<br/> an organized summary of your qualifications. <br/> that a resume gets scanned for 25 seconds. <br/>I should identify accomplishments. </span> </div> \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Resumes & Action Verbs"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " When writing a resume, it is important to show your potential employer all your skills. In order for you to do that, you should use action verbs to help you describe these skills."}, {"type": "text", "content": "A good idea is to start your resume with bullet points with action verbs. It will make your descriptions more powerful. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Here are some action verbs you could use: <ul> <span class=\"italic\"><li>Instead of saying you worked with customers, you could say you \u201c<span class=\"strong\">cemented </span> relationship with customers\u201d</li> <li>It says here you \u201chelped employees\u201d. You could rewrite this as you \u201c<span class=\"strong\">empowered </span> employees through shared decisions\u201d. </li> <li>And don't write that you \u2018dealt with problems'... say \u201cI <span class=\"strong\">solved </span> problems without increasing costs.\u201d</li> </span> </ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "More action verbs are listed below: <ul> <li>created, established, built, diagnosed, boosted, improved. </li> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember to use these verbs in the past. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Other important things to consider when writing your resume are: <ul><li>Format: use a chronological order as it allows you to highlight your experience.</li> <li>Margins: use wide margins </li> <li>Font: Clean type such as Times New Roman or Garamond. </li> <li>Headings: Clear and logical </li> <li>Other: Use<span class=\"strong\"> bold </span> and <span class=\"italic\">italic </span> on areas you want to catch the reader's eye. </li> "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "on point"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "spot on or exactly right"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: What I really liked about the workshop is that the tips were really on point. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob02aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about resumes."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "summary"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a short account giving only the most important  information on something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We want to present a summary of your qualifications."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob02aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to scan"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to read something very quickly in order to get the general idea "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A resume gets scanned for 25 seconds. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob02aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "margin"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the space at the left or right side of a page where words are not written. "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: To begin, use wide margins."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob02aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "format"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the appearance of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: To begin, use a logical format.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob02aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to catch someone's eye"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to get someone's attention"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You need to use bold and italic on areas that you want to catch the reader's eye. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob02aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bullet"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a printed circle before each thing on a list so as to emphasize it"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It is also important to use bullets to emphasize accomplishments."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob02aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to cement"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make an idea or relationship stronger"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I cemented relationships with customers. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob02aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to empower"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to give someone more power to do something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I empowered employees through shared decisions."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob02aud09"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Reread the dialogue."}, {"type":